# Agent execution

Universal, context-free policy. No `.agent-context.json` lookups required.

## Subagents (Task tool)
- Do **not** use the Task tool / subagents unless the user explicitly asks (e.g. "use a subagent", "explore with Task", or named review skills like Bugbot / security-review).
- Prefer Grep, Read, Glob, and Shell in this chat for codebase work.
- Exception: only when the user clearly requests parallel/isolated agents.

## Waiting on commands
- Prefer foreground Shell with a realistic `block_until_ms` (expected runtime + small buffer, usually seconds to a few minutes).
- If backgrounded: one early status check (15–60s), then short polls (30–60s). Cap total silent waiting; after ~2–3 minutes without useful progress, report status and ask whether to keep waiting.
- **Never** set waits / `block_until_ms` to multi-hour maxima for routine lint/test/build.
- Do not poll Task/subagent runs — rely on completion notifications when subagents were explicitly requested.
